{"name":"Dusty Mountain","hex":"#716d63","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Covered with dust.","Powdery and resembling dust."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A medium-brown color.","An old bottle of spirits that has been kept for a long time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusty"},{"term":"mountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An elevation of land of considerable dimensions rising more or less abruptly, forming a conspicuous figure in the landscape, usually having a small extent of surface at its summit. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Something very large in size or quantity; a huge amount; a great heap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusty (Dusty Springfield album)","blocks":[{"text":"Dusty is the second album of singer Dusty Springfield to be released in the US. It was issued on the Philips Records label in 1964 and includes Springfield's hit singles \"All Cried Out\", \"I Just Don't Know What to Do with Myself\" and the double A-side \"Guess Who?\"/\"Live It Up\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/13/Dusty-album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusty_(Dusty_Springfield_album)","wikidata":"Q5317161"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https: